 "final_result": "Built a complete three-script Python workflow for rock-salt LiF band-structure calculations.\n\n**Materials Project ID:** mp-1138, space group Fm-3m (#225).\n\n**Atom count:** 2 atoms in the original CIF (already primitive \u2014 face-centered cubic rock salt has 2 atoms in its primitive cell). After kp_atoms(standard_kpath) reduction: still 2 atoms (Li, F). Space group unchanged.\n\n**Workflow outline:**\n1. **generate_structures.py** \u2014 Reads the primitive LiF cell, writes 51 structures (structure_000.cif unperturbed; 001\u2013050 with T=300 K thermal displacements: Li RMS=0.05 \u00c5, F RMS=0.03 \u00c5, plus up to 1% random lattice strain). LiF is stable at room temperature (melting point ~1165 \u00b0C), so 300 K is well within the stable phase region. Li is lighter (6.94 amu) than F (19.00 amu), so it gets a larger displacement amplitude.\n2. **setup_jobs.py** \u2014 For each structure, creates calculations/NNN/ with pseudopotentials (Li.upf, F.upf), kpath.json (from chem_llm.kpath.standard_kpath), pw.in (SCF), bands.in (NSCF bands), and bands_post.in (bands.x). All pw.x inputs written with ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in; bands.x input with write_fortran_namelist. Key settings: ecutwfc=96 Ry (from Li's 48 Ha recommendation \u00d7 2), ecutrho=384 Ry, occupations='fixed' (insulator, gap ~8.7 eV), conv_thr=1e-8, nspin=1, nbnd=12 (10 total electrons \u2192 5 occupied bands, padded), SCF k-mesh [11,11,11] from scf_kmesh(prim, metal=False), bands k-points from kp_kpts(kp).\n3. **plot_bands.py** \u2014 Reads 000.bands.dat via chem_llm.kpath.plot_axis (validates k-point match), reads pw.out via chem_llm.qe_output.read_pw_out (n_occupied=5, Fermi energy=None as expected for fixed occupations), computes VBM/CBM/gap via band_edges, plots each band per segment (no line across discontinuities), draws tick lines, saves calculations/000/bands_000.pdf.\n\n**ASE functions used:** ase.io.read/write (CIF I/O), ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in (pw.x input), ase.io.espresso.write_fortran_namelist (bands.x input), ase.Atoms (structure representation). No pymatgen imports.\n\n**Band gap obtained:** 8.588 eV (VBM=0.481 eV, CBM=9.069 eV, VBM-aligned). This is close to the Materials Project value of 8.716 eV; the small difference is typical for PBEsol vs. the functional used by MP.\n\n**Scientific assumptions:**\n- Scalar-relativistic pseudopotentials (Li Z=3, F Z=9, both < 54, no spin-orbit physics targeted).\n- Fixed occupations (LiF is a clear insulator with gap > 8 eV).\n- Non-magnetic (moment_per_formula_unit = 0.0).\n- T=300 K displacements are representative of thermal motion in the stable phase.\n- ecutwfc set to the larger of the two element recommendations (Li: 48 Ha > F: 42 Ha).\n\n**Expert review needed:** The perturbed structures (001\u2013050) have not been run through DFT \u2014 only structure_000 was calculated. The displacement amplitudes (0.05 \u00c5 Li, 0.03 \u00c5 F) are estimates based on a rough Debye-temperature argument; a proper molecular dynamics or phonon calculation would give more accurate thermal displacements. The 1% random strain is a simple approximation for thermal expansion fluctuations.",
